# .pluginlintignore — suppress known upstream plugin-lint findings.
#
# Format: <plugin-id-glob> <issue-substring>   # reason
#
# Suppresses a finding only if BOTH the plugin ID matches the glob AND
# the emitted message contains the substring. Keeps upstream issues from
# blocking CI while still reporting regressions in our own code.
#
# Update the REASON column whenever a new entry lands — someone reading
# this file in 6 months should understand why each exception exists.

# Anthropic official plugins — upstream bugs we can't fix here.
claude-plugins-official/huggingface-skills/*  missing YAML frontmatter       # upstream: hugging-face-dataset-viewer SKILL.md lacks frontmatter (report to anthropics/claude-plugins-official)
claude-plugins-official/plugin-dev/*          predictable /tmp paths          # upstream: test-hook.sh example uses $$ pattern (example code; low risk)

# revskills self-suppression — with marketplace source "./" the repo root ships
# as the plugin, so scripts/lint-plugins.sh travels inside the plugin and the
# scanner scans itself. Its comments + one failure-message embed the very
# patterns it detects (not real commands). Scoped to lint-plugins.sh only.
revskills* lint-plugins.sh contains unquoted 'rm -rf $VAR'   # self-match: scanner comment embeds the rm-rf pattern it scans for
revskills* lint-plugins.sh contains 'curl | bash'   # self-match: scanner comment+message embed the curl|bash pattern it scans for
